-MyoConverter is an open-source program that translates OpenSim joints and muscle paths into MJCF, the XML file format that MuJoCo uses to describe a mechanical model \citep{caggiano_myosuite_2022,wang_myosim_2022}. I used it to convert the Gait2392 human model. Figure~\ref{fig:gait2392_human_models} shows how the two programs display the muscle paths on the human skeleton. The converted model reversed two hip actions and assigned eight muscles a maximum active force of only \qty{1}{\newton}. I reversed the affected hinge axes and restored the force scales from OpenSim. At the knee, a misplaced path point prevented the rectus femoris from following the patella as the joint extended. I replaced it with a patella-tracking point from the vastus medialis. These repairs matter because a change in the path can change the torque produced by a given muscle force. Foot contact was set separately. I retained the six foot--ground contact pairs for loaded trials and removed all ground pairs for suspension. Appendix~\ref{sec:app_conversion_repairs} identifies the repaired muscles, the disabled hip rotators, and the joint constraints.
