-I adapted W2L to the Gait2392 human model. In this variant, W2Lvar, PF channels time the activity of motor neurons (MNs), the neurons that recruit muscles. One pair of channels coordinates the hip muscles on each side, and another coordinates the knee and ankle muscles. The circuit contains 888 neurons and 7,868 connected neuron pairs. To change how a knee extensor is recruited, a researcher needs to find the group of motor neurons that drives it, trace the inputs to that group, and inspect the strength and sign of each connection.
